Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Adding an Offset", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.968755536400978*^9, 
  3.968755541909273*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ea66e20d-278d-4174-8515-\
a64a34f7394c"],

Cell["\<\
The summing circuit above can be used to add an offset to a signal. A common \
mistake is to use the power supply to provide a voltage which is then divided \
down to a desired value by a potentiometer (variable resistor). Any noise in \
the power supply is then undesirably passed on to the signal. A better \
approach is to use a precision voltage reference which is a special purpose \
chip designed to produce a very stable and low noise voltage (e.g., 10 V) as \
shown below.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.968755557188094*^9, 
  3.968755570783197*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"f907048a-3bc0-419a-9173-\
b4ca8b69721c"],

