Cell["\<\
We know the uncertainty of the components (resistors are \[PlusMinus]0.1% and \
capacitors are \[PlusMinus]1%) so we can include these in our calculations to \
give uncertainties in the \[Alpha], \[Omega], and \[Zeta]  parameters. We use \
the Mathematica function Around[] to do this. For example, if we have a 0.1% \
1 k\[CapitalOmega] resistor, R,  then we set: \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.969815055989687*^9, 3.969815248087469*^9}, {
  3.969815447340188*^9, 
  3.969815480850423*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"6b585dab-096f-4a7a-82af-\
9a2cd0877728"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"R1", "=", 
  RowBox[{"Around", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"1.", " ", 
     SuperscriptBox["10", "3"]}], ",", 
    RowBox[{"0.001", " ", "1.", " ", 
     SuperscriptBox["10", "3"]}]}], "]"}], " ", 
  RowBox[{"(*", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"1", " ", "k\[CapitalOmega]"}], " ", "\[PlusMinus]", 
    RowBox[{"0.1", "%"}]}], " ", "*)"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.969815254102138*^9, 3.9698152719676*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[156]:=",ExpressionUUID->"74ad2261-d10a-4e87-94f9-c4e71b84cade"],

Cell[BoxData[
 InterpretationBox[
  TemplateBox[{"1000.0", "1.0"},
   "Around"],
  Around[1000., 1.]]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.9698152763026733`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[156]=",ExpressionUUID->"d7baea6b-c330-40ea-9d05-72f629bb825e"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
This gives the expected 1,000 \[CapitalOmega]  \[PlusMinus] 1 \
